   },\n          \"title\": \"Expectation Ids\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"binding_ids\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Binding Ids\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"derivation\": {\n          \"default\": \"\",\n          \"description\": \"This component\\u2019s sourced reasoning; cite accepted IDs instead of repeating their full argument\",\n          \"title\": \"Derivation\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"applicability\": {\n          \"default\": \"\",\n          \"description\": \"Conditions for this component, including any added assumptions or omitted protections\",\n          \"title\": \"Applicability\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"unresolved\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Unresolved\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"conflicts\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Conflicts\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"alternatives\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Alternatives\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Grounding\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"Harness\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"execution_package\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"description\": \"Optional single local Go package or Rust crate directory; the controller fixes the effective package at acceptance\",\n          \"title\": \"Execution Package\"\n        },\n        \"files\": {\n          \"additionalProperties\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"description\": \"Additional generated files with relative destinations and fixed source text\",\n          \"title\": \"Files\",\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        },\n        \"kind\": {\n          \"description\": \"Harness kind advertised by the configured execution backend\",\n          \"title\": \"Kind\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"source\": {\n          \"description\": \"Executable experiment source, calling actual target code; no fabricated expected observations\",\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"title\": \"Source\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"description\": {\n          \"title\": \"Description\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"semantic_changes\": {\n          \"description\": \"Instrumentation and adaptation differences; never alter protocol logic to create a real finding\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Semantic Changes\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"prerequisites\": {\n          \"default\": [],\n          \"items\": {\n            \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/EventRequirement\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Prerequisites\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"legality\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Grounding\",\n          \"default\": {\n            \"source_ids\": [],\n            \"expectation_ids\": [],\n            \"binding_ids\": [],\n            \"derivation\": \"\",\n            \"applicability\": \"\",\n            \"unresolved\": [],\n            \"conflicts\": [],\n            \"alternatives\": []\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"kind\",\n        \"source\",\n        \"description\",\n        \"semantic_changes\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Harness\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"ObservableProperty\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"checker_id\": {\n          \"title\": \"Checker Id\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"kind\": {\n          \"default\": \"event_assertion\",\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"event_assertion\",\n            \"event_implication\"\n          ],\n          \"title\": \"Kind\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"trigger\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Comparison\"\n        },\n        \"assertion\": {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Comparison\"\n        },\n        \"antecedent\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Comparison\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null\n        },\n        \"identity_fields\": {\n          \"description\": \"Independent operation identity shared by prerequisites and result; never the value being compared or a context expected to change\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Identity Fields\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"description\": {\n          \"title\": \"Description\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"checker_id\",\n        \"trigger\",\n        \"assertion\",\n        \"description\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"ObservableProperty\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"description\": \"Concrete investigation of an accepted requirement; execution determines the observed result.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"description\": {\n      \"description\": \"This check\\u2019s discriminator, prefix, controls and observations; reference the accepted claim rather than restating it\",\n      \"title\": \"Description\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"claim_id\": {\n      \"title\": \"Claim Id\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"binding_ids\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Binding Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"harness\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Harness\"\n    },\n    \"monitors\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/EventMonitor\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Monitors\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"observable_properties\": {\n      \"description\": \"Direct route supports event_assertion and event_implication. Correlate prerequisite fields by alias; observe prerequisites and results from the same legal history. Unsupported general temporal properties must remain an explicit limitation.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ObservableProperty\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Observable Properties\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"uncertainties\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Uncertainties\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"description\",\n    \"claim_id\",\n    \"binding_ids\",\n    \"harness\",\n    \"monitors\",\n    \"observable_properties\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"DirectCheckPlan\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/guide.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/references/experiments.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/guide.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/references/experiments.md'","aggregated_output":"SEMANTIC REVIEW Use the supplied contract against fixed inputs, source dependencies and observations. One checker_correspondence review covers requirement, entry/caller duties, oracle, identity, legal history, observation path/completion and counterevidence. For an automatic-continuation claim, check the responsibility source and the inference from finite observations: which producer, consumer, retry, timer or concurrent triggers remain under the stated availability and scheduling assumptions? An unexamined trigger or undrained work remains a gap; neither finite waiting nor a rescue stimulus alone proves lost continuation. Applicability and decomposition need separate answers only for concrete issues. No issue found is provisional, not proof or an independent vote.\n\nCURRENT VERSION Cite unchanged established parts and focus on the increment: what changed, which premise it answers, what the new execution observed and what remains unanswered. Verify that the fixed entry, prefix and schedule still exercise the original discriminator: stronger setup must not exclude the investigated premise. A narrower scope cannot settle its parent; substantive changes use the existing revision rules. New inputs require fresh execution and correspondence; old review success cannot certify them. Scope/cause/consequence questions outside the checked proposition are independent limits, not additional confirmation gates. Never alter a requirement or weaken a predicate merely to obtain a passing test.\n\nISSUES Fixed Claim, Harness and Monitor conflicts have exact issue/condition records. Address the listed issue with a sourced resolution and, where supplied, condition dispositions; do not answer the same conflict separately in several products. A no_issue_found item alone clears nothing. Preserve current counterevidence as an open issue, explained alternatives in rationale and independent limits in limitations. Resolution applies to its answering version and descendants; it does not legalize an older driver. Shared semantic issues follow actual dependencies, not checker names.\n\nREPAIR Distinguish review aspect from challenged component. F4 repairs unreached experiment prerequisites. Ordinary technical repair preserves shared property descriptions, events, identities, predicates and legality; it needs no preliminary review or encoding refactor unless an actual dispute/change requires one. Tool, parser and framework failures are not semantic feedback. Executed harness changes require a new artifact, fresh execution and current correspondence. Driver/configuration/initialization repairs name repair_issue_ids, preserve the requirement and oracle, and replace only sourced current premises. Changed observation/oracle encoding uses explicit correction; changed normative meaning/applicability uses F2, and proposition-preserving dependency expansion uses F3. Resolve against the actual changed component, never an unrelated edit. If additional source evidence answers the issue without changing inputs, resolve on that executed version instead of manufacturing a harness rewrite. Remaining issues and the current version's missing correspondence stay visible independently.\nEXECUTION Observe actual implementation effects under explicit inputs, caller policy and authorized isolation. Contract applicability may remain unresolved during exploration; execution permission may not. Preserve producer history, substitutions and observed completion. A changed value or tests_passed is not a violation oracle. Exploration remains construction knowledge: a later requirement needs a separately fixed check, fresh execution and correspondence review, not retroactive relabelling. Missing capability, compilation failure, timeout, panic and a completed property comparison remain distinct. Retain failures; never precompute expected observations or alter protocol behavior to create a finding.\n\nCOMPLETION Initialization, driver compliance and observation validity belong in prerequisites, controls or diagnostics, not duplicate properties. A diagnostic control need not satisfy the principal scenario's premises or acquire a separate obligation: select formal applicability using independently declared input/policy fields before execution, retaining control output for explanation. If formally comparing distinct scenarios, express each one's actual admission and premises; incompatible histories may need separate checks. Never select scenarios by the observed result, whether reproduction succeeded, or a missing premise after execution. Role or phase readiness does not imply that earlier work has drained. Across preparation, policy changes and delivery, preserve the selected caller/transport contract; prefer one delivery path with policy-selected deferral and record only the identity, provenance and order needed for attribution. Distinguish network receipt, per-message-type queueing and handler dispatch; identify which layer the driver replaces and preserve its ordering constraints, without assuming global FIFO or arbitrary reordering. Legal in-flight work need not be emptied and does not itself invalidate an otherwise supported check. End controlled work independently of the forbidden behavior. Observe admission, completion and final state for the same operation before treating absence as bounded holds. Missing completion, identity, result events and tool timeout remain unknown. A finite tick/wait window records non-completion, not a deadline violation or infinite stalling. For a repeatable suffix, account for behavior-determining state, external schedule, queues, timers and callbacks; equal selected business fields do not close the execution. A later operation restoring progress helps locate a trigger, but may itself be required caller work.\n\nCORRELATION Monitor.admission_alias explicitly selects the declared harness prerequisite admitting operations whose completion is owed. It is not the first prerequisite by array order. Harness.prerequisites contains prerequisite events only; monitors select independent result events. ObservableProperty.identity_fields declares the stable operation identity once, using fields present at the relevant observation points. Do not repeat a result as a prerequisite or duplicate each identity equality as a Comparison. Reference conditions declare necessary predecessor relationships; unrelated prerequisites have no implicit list order. Assertions may refer to any declared prerequisite alias that actually precedes the result. Missing identity/reference fields or nonunique associations remain unknown. Independent applicability is checked before requiring unrelated history. Alias-dependent applicability follows correlation. Each operation is matched separately. A complete violating witness survives missing results in demonstrably independent operations, while coverage remains partial. Same-witness ambiguity and potentially global parse loss still block attribution. Use independent identity, not the compared value, to associate an input and output. A context expected to change cannot also be an equality filter. More complex histories need actual correlated prerequisites and results; unsupported general temporal expressions remain a stated limitation.\n\nMEANING Record comparisons in properties/outcome and scope/applicability limits separately. Identify whether decisive observations read a live object, copy, cache or caller-maintained state; an export discrepancy need not mean the active protocol state changed. Verify the observation path as required by the claim, without mandatory dual observation or private-state access. Keep unresolved contracts, counterevidence, input legality and observation differences explicit; CheckRun owns execution status. An implementation/requirement discrepancy is the investigation subject, not a conflict between requirement sources. Real contradictions remain conflicts.\n\nCONFIRMATION Review a direct check as a whole against its accepted obligation, actual calls, adaptations, event parsing, correlated prerequisites and independent oracle. A completed measured comparison survives wider-history and excluded-consequence limits, but cannot establish a broader consequence; missing correspondence keeps attribution pending without erasing the measurement. Judge instrumentation and substitutes from the supplied code and stopping point instead of a language-specific syntax rule. Construct a direct check with actual observations; equal checker IDs alone are insufficient. Unsupported expressions or incomplete histories remain gaps. Preserve unresolved semantic disputes. Newly recovered implementation knowledge may first be saved with a specific applicability issue, without automatically changing the requirement or scope.\nREACHABILITY Separate the requirement's source and applicability, the consumer effect under controlled input, actual producer execution and same-history correlation, and the observed system endpoint. A call edge or constructible input does not execute its producer. Two isolated fragments do not establish one legal protocol history. Name substituted edges, fault assumptions and identity/context/generation continuity. Retain wider consequences as limits unless their endpoint is observed. A permitted pending path cannot be called a safety violation merely because an equality oracle expected success.\nNECESSITY For a sourced safety condition S implies E, compare observed S only when independently established E is false, or use an equivalent supported implication encoding. Do not silently strengthen it to S equals E, suppress the result field through applicability, or infer eventual success from a permitted pending control.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
