{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"head -85 ../agent-source/omnipaxos_runtime/src/handle.rs; grep -R -n 'admission_alias\\\\|reference.*\\\\.' /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources | head -30; nl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos_runtime/src/traits.rs | tail -25\"","aggregated_output":"use core::time::Duration;\nuse std::marker::PhantomData;\n\nuse futures::channel::oneshot;\n\nuse omnipaxos::{\n    messages::Message,\n    storage::{Entry, Storage},\n    util::{LogEntry, NodeId},\n    ClusterConfig, OmniPaxos,\n};\n\nuse super::{\n    actor::{run, ActorConfig, ActorState},\n    event::{AppendError, Command, OmniPaxosEvent, RuntimeProposeErr},\n    traits::{ActorEntry, AsyncRuntime},\n};\n\n/// Configuration for the async runtime actor.\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\npub struct RuntimeConfig {\n    /// How often the actor calls `tick()` on the underlying OmniPaxos.\n    /// Should match the tick timeout budget used when building `ServerConfig`.\n    pub tick_period: Duration,\n    /// How often outgoing messages are drained and forwarded on the `outgoing_messages`\n    /// channel.\n    pub egress_period: Duration,\n    /// Bounded capacity for the actor's command channel.\n    pub cmd_channel_capacity: usize,\n    /// Bounded capacity for the outgoing message channel.\n    pub outgoing_capacity: usize,\n    /// Bounded capacity for the incoming message channel.\n    pub incoming_capacity: usize,\n    /// Bounded capacity for the event channel.\n    pub event_capacity: usize,\n    /// How long an `append_notify` call waits for its entry to be decided before\n    /// resolving with [`AppendError::Timeout`](super::AppendError::Timeout).\n    pub append_notify_timeout: Duration,\n    /// Bounded capacity for each per-subscriber decided-log stream returned by\n    /// [`OmniPaxosHandle::subscribe_decided`].\n    pub decided_channel_capacity: usize,\n    /// Maximum number of concurrently outstanding `append_notify` calls (i.e.\n    /// calls that have not yet resolved). Once reached, further `append_notify`\n    /// calls are rejected immediately with [`AppendError::TooManyOutstanding`]\n    /// rather than queued, so a stalled cluster (e.g. no leader) can't grow this\n    /// backlog without bound.\n    pub max_pending_appends: usize,\n    /// Maximum number of concurrent [`OmniPaxosHandle::subscribe_decided`]\n    /// subscribers. Once reached, a new subscription is rejected: the returned\n    /// receiver's channel is closed immediately without delivering any entries.\n    pub max_decided_subscribers: usize,\n    /// Fallback cap on how many outgoing messages the actor buffers internally\n    /// while waiting for room on the (bounded) `outgoing_messages` channel,\n    /// used only if that channel's own capacity can't be read. Past this cap,\n    /// the *oldest* buffered messages are dropped rather than growing without\n    /// bound -- safe because OmniPaxos already tolerates lost messages via its\n    /// own resend/retry mechanisms.\n    pub max_outgoing_buffered: usize,\n}\n\nimpl Default for RuntimeConfig {\n    fn default() -> Self {\n        Self {\n            tick_period: Duration::from_millis(10),\n            egress_period: Duration::from_millis(1),\n            cmd_channel_capacity: 1024,\n            outgoing_capacity: 10_000,\n            incoming_capacity: 10_000,\n            event_capacity: 1024,\n            append_notify_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n            decided_channel_capacity: 1024,\n            max_pending_appends: 1024,\n            max_decided_subscribers: 128,\n            max_outgoing_buffered: 10_000,\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// A cloneable, `Send + Sync` handle to an OmniPaxos actor running in the background.\n///\n/// All state-mutating and read methods are `async`. Users must drive message transport\n/// externally via [`OmniPaxosHandle::outgoing_messages`] and\n/// [`OmniPaxosHandle::handle_incoming`]. Dropping every clone shuts the actor down.\npub struct OmniPaxosHandle<T>\nwhere\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/tasks/audit.md:12:- check / revise_check: select unit_id (or its Candidate alias), or create an obligation through candidate. Supply plan_path, draft-source harness_path and optional destination-to-draft files; plan.harness.execution_package may select one Go package or Rust crate for this check. Metadata source/files stay empty; the controller fixes executable bytes and adapter support. Never replace target code or dependencies. Revisions name previous_check_id. Driver legality repairs name repair_issue_ids and explain changed inputs and sources; reference every removed conflict's exact issue. Changed executed checker encoding uses encoding_revision.\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/tasks/audit.md:14:- review: select artifact_id; omitted item target_id inherits it. Carries feedback, not a map. Use review_contracts/review_questions: Direct Check requires checker_correspondence; other aspects are optional unless resolving an issue of that aspect. revision_needed names challenged_components. Resolve exact issue_ids using acquired Material source_ids, a concise answer and retained evidence_ids when relevant. For supplied conditions, use condition_dispositions with exact condition_id, sources and applicability; current_judgment remains unresolved. Unchanged sources and reasoning can be referenced, not recopied. The review guide defines semantic criteria. Candidate applicability review creates no execution Evidence.\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/tasks/audit.md:30:Claim/Scope owns requirement and applicability; Harness legality records this history and caller duties. Before constructing a harness, inspect the selected entry's actual initialization and shutdown/resource lifecycle; before comparing results, record or check that the necessary prerequisites occurred. A process PASS is not a prerequisite witness. If setup was not reached, retain the observation and minimally repair the harness without changing the discriminator. Use the evidence-review guide and experiments reference for independent monitoring, identity, completion and attribution; initialization alone does not establish legal history. claim.concern classifies responsibility, not confidence.\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/guide.md:19:At handoffs identify the answered proposition, supporting sources/execution and independent remaining question in feedback. At the next substantive product already updating the relevant Behavior, Fact or overview, or preparing a Candidate that relies on that knowledge, replace the answered original sentence with its sourced conditional relationship and remove obsolete execution/review reminders. Preserve independent unknowns and historical inputs. Consult the actual answer and assessment; an understanding label or exact reference does not establish resolution. Correct misleading explanations before reuse, without a dedicated cleanup turn or unrelated whole-map sweep. Source reading and exploration may continue from feedback; near expiry save minimal complete learning. Use behavior-facts.md for field ownership and tasks/audit.md for product references.\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/SKILL.md:8:Use [guide.md](guide.md). Only controller-loaded references are available; links do not grant file access. Use Codex tools for missing authorized source; submit a typed research product only when ready for validation.\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/references/experiments.md:5:CORRELATION Monitor.admission_alias explicitly selects the declared harness prerequisite admitting operations whose completion is 